WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.070
You can tell a lot about a country

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.270
from its passport.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.390
Color is the first giveaway.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.080
Nations tend to pick colors

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.190
that reflect their national character.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.850
New Zealand decorates
its famous rugby team,

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.540
its airline, and its passports

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.080
in the nation's favorite color, black.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.840
Many Islamic countries
have green passports

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.790
because of the importance of
the color in the Muslim faith.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.540
But as well as a statement
of national identity,

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:38.030
color can demonstrate
international cooperation.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:44.620
The British passport was
originally a regal navy blue.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:49.090
But after Britain joined
the European Union in 1973,

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:53.320
it switched to burgundy red in
line with other EU countries.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.520
The common color was supposed to make

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.240
European passports instantly recognizable.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.230
But since colors can't be patented,

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:05.940
nothing stops other with the same idea.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.250
A number of countries
that aspire to join the EU

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.510
have changed their
passports to burgundy too.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:17.880
Meanwhile, Britain has
decided to leave the club.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.080
Its government has announced
that the UK passports

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:24.000
will revert back to
navy blue after Brexit.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.260
If you have a passport from
Singapore or South Korea,

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.710
you're in position of
one of the most powerful

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:34.580
travel documents on earth.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:39.010
Passport power is measured
by the number of countries

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.340
the holder can access visa-free.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.960
Currently sharing first
place in the power rankings,

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.740
Singaporean and South Korean passports

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:53.250
provide visa-free access
to 162 countries each.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.470
British passport holders
share fourth place

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:00.680
in the power ranking
with six other nations,

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.190
each accessing 159 countries visa-free.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:08.640
Americans rank fifth with access to 158.

00:02:09.585 --> 00:02:13.460
Somalia, Syria, Pakistan, and Iraq

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.160
are among the world's
least powerful passports.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.810
Afghanistan is the lowest-ranking of all,

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:23.010
with visa-free access
to just 26 countries.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.180
Having to get a visa is a hassle.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.240
First, there is the never-ending form.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:33.810
Then there are lengthy
appointments and expensive fees.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.340
Some visas also require
travelers to pre-book flights

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.420
to prove that they intend to return home.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.680
But there are unexpected upsides

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.680
to some of the world's weaker passports.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:51.640
Middle-ranking Namibia is one
of just a handful of countries

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.440
whose citizens can enter Angola visa-free.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:58.490
India is one of only three countries

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:01.160
whose citizens have
visa-free access into Bhutan.

00:03:03.068 --> 00:03:06.240
A low-ranking passport
limits your choices,

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.430
but not your sense of adventure.

